testdata/slowtool/
testdata/mutants/

# Compiled binaries.
#
# `go build` names its output after the directory, so a build inside ch05/
# leaves ch05/ch05, and `go build -o bin` leaves ch05/bin. The exercise SOURCE
# under ch0* IS tracked -- the grader compiles and drives it, and it is the
# only thing that proves the public API is usable from outside the module.
# Only the build output belongs here.
#
# This was previously spelled `/ch0`, which matched NOTHING: gitignore does
# not prefix-match without a wildcard, so `/ch0` matches only a root entry
# named exactly "ch0". Three 9MB binaries were committed while that rule
# looked like it was working.
#
# These patterns are deliberately depth-independent. From Chapter 5 on, a
# submission is repo-root-shaped (agent/ + chNN/), so a snapshot under
# solutions/ nests a SECOND copy of the whole layout: solutions/ch07/ch05/bin
# is a real path. Depth-anchored spellings like `solutions/*/bin` cannot keep
# up with that, and two binaries were staged before this was fixed. A pattern
# with no slash matches at any depth; `**/` means the same thing explicitly.
#
# The graders BUILD these binaries into the submission tree every time they
# run, so deleting them by hand does not keep them gone. Only the ignore rule
# does.
bin
**/ch0*/ch0*

# Agent working directories: tool output and scratch, created by any manual
# run. Run OUTPUT, not source.
cr/

# Event logs are run OUTPUT, not source. Tracking one meant every manual run of
# a solution showed up as a modification and added noise to every git status.
# The rule covers *.log rather than one filename because the default log name is
# derived from the executable: a binary built from solutions/ch03 writes
# ch03.log, and one you named yourself writes whatever you named it.
*.log
